    "title": "Editor's Corner: It's time for gender neutral language - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Galeta Sandercock ,\n1 days ago On Feb. 27, 2023, College Government Senators unanimously passed the Gender Inclusivity Ballot Question, giving students the opportunity, through a non-binding referendum, to indicate their stance on policies of gender inclusivity at Wellesley. The questions concerned both the College’s admissions policy and its use of gendered language in official communications. In a Mar. 6, 2023 email, President Paula Johnson affirmed “Wellesley’s mission as a women’s college,” vehemently denying that there will be any change to the admissions policy and making it clear there were no plans of transitioning away from gendered language. However, she announced a commitment to “supporting,” “acknowledging” and “respecting” trans and non-binary students. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
